---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="About" description="Why Tahoe Public Meetings exists and who built it.">
  <section class="page-hero compact"><div class="section-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">SITE INFORMATION</p><h1>About</h1></div></section>
  <section class="section-wrap content-section about-content">
    <div class="about-prose">
      <p>Lake Tahoe has a whole lot of public agencies, each with regular meetings discussing important topics. It can be tricky to keep up with them all! I built this website to help me keep track of upcoming agenda items that I want to follow. I hope it can be useful to you too! If you have ideas that could make it more useful to you too, please <button class="inline-feedback" type="button" data-feedback-open>let me know</button>!</p>
      <p>This site was built by Nick Speal as a personal hobby project. No guarantees are offered as to the accuracy or timeliness of the information presented. It is still a new project under active development, so expect many bugs! Again, I'd love to hear <button class="inline-feedback" type="button" data-feedback-open>feedback</button>. See the <a href="/coverage/">Coverage</a> page for the data sources used.</p>
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>I count page views with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, an open-source tool with no cookies and no stored IP addresses, so I can see which pages and links people use. Each visit gets a random code that expires after eight hours, so I can tell which pages are viewed together, but not who you are or whether you've been here before. Nothing is shared with advertisers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
